# Performance

Treat battery, memory, and jank as product bugs.

## Requirements

- No unnecessary re-renders (isolate timers; don’t tick whole trees at 500ms)
- Lazy load routes and heavy folders
- Virtual scrolling for long lists
- Memoization only where it prevents real work (follow React Compiler guidance; don’t spam useMemo)
- Cache + prefetch thoughtfully; batch requests
- Code split / tree shake; remove unused deps
- Optimize images, icons, fonts
- Compress responses (platform CDN); keep Vite chunks lean
- Minimize GPS: one watch when possible, raise `maximumAge`, pause on `visibilityState === hidden`, throttle localStorage + session events
- Animations ≤200ms; always honor reduce-motion

## Driver GPS

- Prefer shared / throttled telemetry persistence (seconds or Δmiles), not every fix
- High accuracy only when moving / active delivery; idle can degrade
- Never keep dual high-accuracy watches without reason

## Definition of done

A performance change is incomplete if it increases battery drain, doubles render frequency, or grows the critical path bundle without measurement.
